<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Colvile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1907">1907</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir Henry Edward Colvile</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Colvile was a British army officer who served as acting commissioner of the Uganda <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> from 1893 to 1895. At the end of 1893 he led British-officered troops and a large Ganda army into Bunyoro against Omukama <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabalega">Kabalega</a>, occupying much of the kingdom and building forts. He later commanded a division in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a> and was removed after the surrender at Lindley in 1900.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-colvile.jpg" alt="Henry Colvile" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: not identified · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burnham_churchill_jul1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
